   "source": [
    "# Celery + Redis + Flower — Hands-On\n",
    "\n",
    "**TechBot scenario:** Handle 50 concurrent user requests without blocking the API server.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:**\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "docker run -d --name redis-stack -p 6379:6379 -p 8001:8001 redis/redis-stack:latest\n",
    "pip install celery[redis] flower fastapi uvicorn httpx\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**IMPORTANT:** Celery workers must be started from the terminal (not inside Jupyter).\n",
    "This notebook shows the code structure + lets you call tasks. Run workers in a separate terminal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Understand the File Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "Celery requires importable Python modules. The full project structure is in `05_chatbot_project/`.\n",
    "Here we show the code inline for learning purposes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# celery_app.py — This file configures the Celery application\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# (shown inline for explanation; saved as a real file in 05_chatbot_project/)\n",
    "\n",
    "REDIS_URL = \"redis://localhost:6379/0\"\n",
    "\n",
    "celery_config = {\n",
    "    # Serialization — JSON is human-readable and debuggable\n",
    "    \"task_serializer\":    \"json\",\n",
    "    \"result_serializer\":  \"json\",\n",
    "    \"accept_content\":     [\"json\"],\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Reliability\n",
    "    # task_acks_late=True: worker ACKs AFTER completing (not on pickup)\n",
    "    # If worker crashes mid-task, task is re-queued\n",
    "    \"task_acks_late\":               True,\n",
    "    \"task_reject_on_worker_lost\":   True,\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Visibility timeout MUST be > longest task duration\n",
    "    # LLM inference can take minutes — set conservatively\n",
    "    \"broker_transport_options\":     {\"visibility_timeout\": 7200},  # 2 hours\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Result storage\n",
    "    \"result_expires\":               86400,  # keep results 24 hours\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # GPU workers: 1 task at a time, no prefetch\n",
    "    \"worker_prefetch_multiplier\":   1,\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Prevent memory leaks (large models accumulate garbage)\n",
    "    \"worker_max_tasks_per_child\":   100,\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Safety limits on runaway tasks\n",
    "    \"task_soft_time_limit\":         540,   # SIGTERM at 9 minutes\n",
    "    \"task_time_limit\":              600,   # SIGKILL at 10 minutes\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Route by task name to dedicated queues\n",
    "    \"task_routes\": {\n",
    "        \"tasks.inference.run_inference\":       {\"queue\": \"gpu\"},\n",
    "        \"tasks.embedding.generate_embedding\":  {\"queue\": \"cpu\"},\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Celery configuration:\")\n",
    "for k, v in celery_config.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: {v}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Define Tasks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# TASK DEFINITIONS (these belong in tasks/inference.py)\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "# We create a minimal Celery app here for demonstration\n",
    "from celery import Celery\n",
    "\n",
    "demo_app = Celery(\n",
    "    \"demo_tasks\",\n",
    "    broker=REDIS_URL,\n",
    "    backend=REDIS_URL,\n",
    ")\n",
    "demo_app.conf.update(**celery_config)\n",
    "demo_app.conf.task_routes = {}  # clear routes for demo (no gpu/cpu split needed)\n",
    "\n",
    "@demo_app.task(bind=True, max_retries=3, default_retry_delay=5)\n",
    "def slow_task(self, n: int, delay: float = 1.0):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Demo task that simulates LLM inference.\n",
    "    bind=True gives access to self.retry() for retry logic.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    import time\n",
    "    import random\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Simulate occasional failures (to test retry)\n",
    "    if random.random() < 0.1:  # 10% chance of failure\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Simulated failure for task {n}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    time.sleep(delay)\n",
    "    return {\"input\": n, \"result\": n * n, \"worker_pid\": __import__('os').getpid()}\n",
    "\n",
    "@demo_app.task\n",
    "def add_numbers(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simple fast task — for the cpu queue.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return a + b\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Tasks registered:\")\n",
    "for name in demo_app.tasks:\n",
    "    if not name.startswith(\"celery.\"):\n",
    "        print(f\"  {name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Start a Worker\n",
    "\n",
    "Open a NEW terminal and run:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "cd /home/hex/Documents/devops/dev-bits-daily\n",
    "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
    "\n",
    "# Start a worker that processes the default queue\n",
    "celery -A redis.04_celery_flower.02_hands_on:demo_app worker \\\n",
    "  --concurrency=4 \\\n",
    "  --pool=prefork \\\n",
    "  --loglevel=info\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Then come back to this notebook and continue.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Also start Flower in another terminal:**\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "celery -A redis.04_celery_flower.02_hands_on:demo_app flower --port=5555\n",
    "```\n",
    "Open http://localhost:5555 to see tasks in real-time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Submit Tasks and Check Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "from celery.result import AsyncResult\n",
    "\n",
    "# Submit a single task\n",
    "task = slow_task.delay(5, delay=0.5)\n",
    "print(f\"Task submitted. ID: {task.id}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Task state: {task.state}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Wait for result\n",
    "print(\"Waiting for result...\")\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    result = task.get(timeout=10)  # wait up to 10 seconds\n",
    "    print(f\"Result: {result}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"State: {task.state}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Task failed: {e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Submit multiple tasks concurrently and poll for results\n",
    "print(\"Submitting 10 tasks concurrently...\")\n",
    "start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Submit all 10 — returns immediately (O(1) per submit)\n",
    "task_ids = []\n",
    "for i in range(10):\n",
    "    t = slow_task.delay(i, delay=1.0)  # each takes 1 second\n",
    "    task_ids.append(t.id)\n",
    "    print(f\"  Submitted task {i}: {t.id[:16]}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "submit_time = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAll 10 submitted in {submit_time*1000:.0f}ms\")\n",
    "print(\"Workers process them in parallel (if concurrency > 1)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Poll until all tasks are complete\n",
    "# This simulates what a FastAPI endpoint's polling mechanism does\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPolling for results...\")\n",
    "poll_start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "pending = set(task_ids)\n",
    "completed = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "while pending:\n",
    "    for task_id in list(pending):\n",
    "        result_obj = AsyncResult(task_id, app=demo_app)\n",
    "        if result_obj.ready():\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                val = result_obj.get()\n",
    "                completed[task_id] = {\"status\": \"SUCCESS\", \"result\": val}\n",
    "            except Exception as e:\n",
    "                completed[task_id] = {\"status\": \"FAILURE\", \"error\": str(e)}\n",
    "            pending.remove(task_id)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if pending:\n",
    "        print(f\"  Waiting... {len(pending)} tasks still running\")\n",
    "        time.sleep(0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "total_time = time.perf_counter() - poll_start\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAll {len(completed)} tasks completed in {total_time:.1f}s\")\n",
    "successes = sum(1 for v in completed.values() if v['status'] == 'SUCCESS')\n",
    "failures = len(completed) - successes\n",
    "print(f\"Successes: {successes}, Failures: {failures}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nNote: with 4 concurrent workers and 1s tasks, 10 tasks take ~{10/4:.0f}s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: FastAPI Integration Pattern\n",
    "\n",
    "This shows how TechBot's API endpoints work. (Run this cell to see the code; to actually run it, use uvicorn from the terminal.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fastapi_code = '''\n",
    "# main.py — TechBot FastAPI gateway\n",
    "from fastapi import FastAPI, BackgroundTasks\n",
    "from celery.result import AsyncResult\n",
    "from tasks.inference import run_inference  # real task from 05_chatbot_project\n",
    "\n",
    "api = FastAPI(title=\"TechBot API\")\n",
    "\n",
    "@api.post(\"/chat\")\n",
    "async def submit_chat(session_id: str, message: str):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Accepts a user message and submits it as a Celery task.\n",
    "    Returns immediately with a task_id — no waiting for LLM.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    task = run_inference.apply_async(\n",
    "        args=[session_id, message],\n",
    "        queue=\"gpu\",          # GPU worker queue\n",
    "        priority=5,           # normal priority (0-9)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    # Returns in < 10ms regardless of inference time\n",
    "    return {\"task_id\": task.id, \"status\": \"queued\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@api.get(\"/task/{task_id}\")\n",
    "async def get_task_result(task_id: str):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Client polls this every 500ms to check if the response is ready.\n",
    "    Returns PENDING while inference is running, SUCCESS when done.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    result = AsyncResult(task_id)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if result.state == \"PENDING\":\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"PENDING\"}\n",
    "    elif result.state == \"STARTED\":\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"STARTED\"}\n",
    "    elif result.state == \"SUCCESS\":\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"SUCCESS\", **result.get()}\n",
    "    elif result.state == \"FAILURE\":\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"FAILURE\", \"error\": str(result.result)}\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return {\"status\": result.state}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run with:\n",
    "# uvicorn main:api --host 0.0.0.0 --port 9000 --reload\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "print(fastapi_code)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Monitor with Flower\n",
    "\n",
    "If Flower is running (from Step 3), open http://localhost:5555\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to look for:**\n",
    "- **Workers tab:** See your worker(s) listed with status Online/Offline\n",
    "- **Tasks tab:** Real-time feed of tasks — PENDING → STARTED → SUCCESS\n",
    "- **Monitor tab:** Graphs of task throughput\n",
    "- **Queues tab:** Current queue lengths (backlog)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Simulate load to see Flower in action:**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Send a burst of 20 tasks to make Flower show activity\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Sending 20 tasks to make Flower show activity...\")\n",
    "print(\"Check http://localhost:5555 now!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "burst_tasks = []\n",
    "for i in range(20):\n",
    "    t = slow_task.delay(i, delay=0.3)\n",
    "    burst_tasks.append(t)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"20 tasks submitted. Waiting for all to complete...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Wait for all\n",
    "for t in burst_tasks:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        t.get(timeout=30)\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"All done. Check Flower for the task history.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Worker Pool Options Explained"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "worker_options = \"\"\"\n",
    "WORKER POOL OPTIONS:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. prefork (default)\n",
    "   celery worker --pool=prefork --concurrency=8\n",
    "   - Forks N child processes\n",
    "   - Each child handles one task at a time\n",
    "   - Best for CPU-bound tasks\n",
    "   - DANGER: Do NOT use with CUDA/GPU (fork is not CUDA-safe)\n",
    "\n",
    "2. solo\n",
    "   celery worker --pool=solo --concurrency=1\n",
    "   - Single process, no forking\n",
    "   - Only one task at a time\n",
    "   - REQUIRED for GPU workers (CUDA-safe)\n",
    "   - GPU can only run 1 inference at a time anyway\n",
    "\n",
    "3. threads\n",
    "   celery worker --pool=threads --concurrency=8\n",
    "   - Uses Python threads instead of processes\n",
    "   - Good for I/O-bound tasks (HTTP calls, DB queries)\n",
    "   - Python GIL limits CPU parallelism\n",
    "\n",
    "4. gevent / eventlet\n",
    "   celery worker --pool=gevent --concurrency=1000\n",
    "   - Coroutine-based (green threads)\n",
    "   - Massive concurrency for I/O-bound tasks\n",
    "   - Requires: pip install gevent\n",
    "\n",
    "FOR TECHBOT:\n",
    "  GPU inference workers:  --pool=solo --concurrency=1\n",
    "  CPU embedding workers:  --pool=prefork --concurrency=4\n",
    "  Notification workers:   --pool=gevent --concurrency=100\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "print(worker_options)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cleanup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clear Celery result keys from Redis\n",
    "import redis as redis_lib\n",
    "\n",
    "r_raw = redis_lib.Redis(host=\"localhost\", port=6379, decode_responses=True)\n",
    "patterns = [\"celery-task-meta-*\", \"_kombu*\", \"unacked*\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for pat in patterns:\n",
    "    keys = list(r_raw.scan_iter(pat))\n",
    "    if keys:\n",
    "        r_raw.delete(*keys)\n",
    "        print(f\"Deleted {len(keys)} keys matching '{pat}'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Cleanup done.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Component | Role | Redis Key Pattern |\n",
    "|-----------|------|------------------|\n",
    "| Celery Broker | Task queue | `_kombu.binding.{queue}` |\n",
    "| Result Backend | Task results | `celery-task-meta-{task_id}` |\n",
    "| Flower | Monitoring dashboard | Reads from broker |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Worker selection guide:**\n",
    "- GPU tasks (vLLM inference): `--pool=solo --concurrency=1`\n",
    "- CPU tasks (embeddings): `--pool=prefork --concurrency=N`\n",
    "- I/O tasks (notifications): `--pool=gevent --concurrency=100`\n",
    "\n",
    "Next: **05_chatbot_project/** — The complete TechBot combining all modules."
   ]
  }
